# hsm-sim 0.1.0: watermarks
# A 3000 MB burst arrives at 10 MB/s into a 2000 MB cache, while the single
# drive writes tape at only 5 MB/s. Nothing is old enough to migrate by age,
# so once the cache crosses its high watermark with nothing purgeable the
# system migrates early ("pressure"). Purging can only free data that is
# already on tape, so while the cache is full of resident files, writes are
# rejected. Migration hands the drive batches of at most batch_mb, and each
# batch can be purged as soon as it lands. Compare the peak cache use with
# the rejected-write count.
# cache 2000 MB, watermarks 85% high / 60% low
# 1 drive(s), 3 tape(s) x 10000 MB, mount 60 s, seek 15 s, 5 MB/s
# scan every 600 s, migrate after 3000 s in batches of 300 MB, auto-repack off

